# Document Routing Rules

## Purpose

These rules define where each document semantic type should live so long-lived truth, current tasks, and one-off changes do not get mixed together.

## Semantic routes

- `workflow.intake` -> `docs/workflow/00-intake/README.md`
- `workflow.requirements` -> `docs/workflow/01-requirements/README.md`
- `workflow.design` -> `docs/workflow/02-design/README.md`
- `workflow.implementation` -> `docs/workflow/03-implementation/README.md`
- `workflow.verification` -> `docs/workflow/04-verification/README.md`
- `workflow.tasks` -> `docs/workflow/05-tasks/README.md`
- `knowledge.context` -> `docs/knowledge/context/`
- `knowledge.structure` -> `docs/knowledge/structure/`
- `knowledge.behavior` -> `docs/knowledge/behavior/`
- `knowledge.reference` -> `docs/knowledge/reference/`
- `changes.active` -> `docs/changes/active/<change-key>/`
- `changes.completed` -> `docs/changes/completed/`
- `changes.legacy` -> `docs/changes/legacy/`
- `records.issues` -> `docs/issues/`
- `records.releases` -> `docs/releases/`
- `records.decisions` -> `docs/adr/`
- `records.archive` -> `docs/archive/`

## Quick routing guide

- Why this version exists, what it delivers, how it works now, how it is verified, and what comes next: use `workflow`
- Long-lived facts, glossary, structure, rules, and reusable examples: use `knowledge`
- A single requirement change or bug-fix workspace: use `changes`
- Issues, releases, decisions, and retired docs: use `records`
- Record documents must follow `docs/rules/document-archive-rules.md`, use `TYPE-YYYYMMDD-NNN`, and archive by year and month
- Long-lived state documents keep fixed paths; when they grow large, split them by feature module and keep the directory-level `README.md` as the index

## Phase Mapping

| Phase | Route |
|---|---|
| specify | `workflow.intake`, `workflow.requirements` |
| clarify | open-question sections in intake / requirements, and `records.issues` when needed |
| plan | `workflow.design`, `workflow.implementation`, `workflow.verification`, `knowledge.*` |
| tasks | `workflow.tasks`, `changes.active` |
| analyze | `workflow.requirements`, `workflow.design`, `workflow.verification`, `workflow.tasks`, `changes.active` |
| implement | code, tests, scripts, migrations; task source still traces to `workflow.tasks` |
| converge | `workflow.*`, `knowledge.*`, `changes.completed`, `records.*` |

Note: this borrows Spec Kit's phase rhythm without making `specs/` the default long-term document directory.

## Sync requirements

- If the directory structure changes, update `spec-init.topology.yml`
- If new routing rules are added, update this file and `README.md`
